AB  - Data hiding (DH) is a technique that hides the existence of sensitive information from the malicious users. In this paper, a novel dynamic block selection (DBS) and DH methods with image encryption (IE) has been developed to improve the embedding capacity (EC), and quality of the stego image. Initially, optimal pixels (OP) is found using fruit fly optimization hybridized improved seeker (FOIS) algorithm. The OP is grouped together with the intensity and pixel value difference (PVD) with its nearest OP. Pixel sorting value (PSV) is a method to shuffle the pixel value (PV) which improves the performance. The different DH along with weight based data embedding (WDE) capacity predictions are achieved by hiding the secret data in each block by using Most Significant Bit (MSB) and least significant bit (LSB) techniques. The data security is improved by rivest cipher (RC4) encryption and the IE is achieved using bit plane encryption (BPE) method. The experimental results show that the proposed method performs better than existing state-of-the-art methods. Further, it can resist the regular singular (RS) and it pixel differencing histogram (PDH) analysis. © 2023, The Author(s), under exclusive licence to Bharati Vidyapeeth's Institute of Computer Applications and Management.
