AB  - The increasing demand for secure multimedia communication has driven the evolution of steganographic techniques beyond single-media approaches. This paper presents a novel hybrid steganography framework that integrates data hiding across multiple media types-images, audio, and video-while employing genetic algorithm optimization for embedding position selection and machine learning-based packet manipulation detection. The proposed system utilizes media-specific embedding strategies: LSB modification for images, phase coding for audio, and motion vector adjustment for video, unified under an adaptive framework with XOR encryption. Genetic algorithm optimization enhances imperceptibility by intelligently selecting embedding positions based on perceptual significance and robustness criteria. The integrated machine learning component provides real-Time packet manipulation detection with 98.7% accuracy, ensuring communication channel integrity. Experimental evaluation on benchmark datasets demonstrates superior performance with PSNR values exceeding 45 dB for images, SNR above 35 dB for audio, and motion distortion below 2% for video. The system achieves an extraction accuracy of 99.5% under various attack scenarios while maintaining computational efficiency suitable for real-Time applications. Comparative analysis reveals \mathbf{2 5-4 0 \% improvement in robustness over traditional single-media steganographic methods. © 2025 IEEE.
