AB  - This study introduces a novel steganographic framework that fuses Cuckoo Search optimization with chaotic maps and Lévy flights to improve security and imperceptibility in LSB embedding. By guiding pixel selection through chaotic behavior and Lévy-driven exploration, the method minimizes detectability while maintaining computational efficiency. Three core contributions define this work. First, among the chaotic systems evaluated, the Henon map offers the best tradeoff between capacity and stealth, achieving a fitness score of 0.67. Second, the Lévy-enhanced approach reduces pixel modifications by 1 5-4 0 \% compared to non-Lévy methods. Third, the system achieves strong imperceptibility, with a PSNR of 68.74 dB for 64 bit payloads and a 63 % reduction in modification variance. A 39% narrower modification range further confirms its robustness against statistical detection. These results demonstrate a secure and adaptive solution for high-capacity steganography, particularly suited to sensitive applications.  © 2025 IEEE.
